gpui: a bad frame ends a GIF or WebP load

A frame that did not decode was skipped and the loop asked for the
next; on a damaged file the decoder may never stop. The load now ends
with the decoder's error (Ely C14.7). Since 0.3.12 GIF and WebP share
one frame loop, and errors no longer name the source.

diff --git a/vendor/gpui-pre/src/platform.rs b/vendor/gpui-pre/src/platform.rs
--- a/vendor/gpui-pre/src/platform.rs
+++ b/vendor/gpui-pre/src/platform.rs
@@ -3494,14 +3494,13 @@ fn decode_animated_frames<'a>(
                 }
                 frames.push(frame);
             }
-            Err(err) => {
-                log::debug!("Skipping {format_name} frame due to decode error: {err}");
-            }
+            // A bad frame ends it: the decoder may never stop.
+            Err(err) => return Err(err.into()),
         }
     }
 
     if frames.is_empty() {
-        anyhow::bail!("{format_name} could not be decoded: all frames failed");
+        anyhow::bail!("{format_name} could not be decoded: no frames");
     }
 
     Ok(frames)
